 "summary": "KIF is a Lisp-syntax first-order logic language with meta-level quotation designed in the DARPA Knowledge Sharing Effort for interchanging knowledge between systems; it evolved into ISO/IEC 24707 Common Logic, an abstract syntax and model-theoretic semantics with concrete dialects CLIF (KIF-like), CGIF and XCL.",
